    "description": "Vintage Glass Telegraph & Telephone Insulators\nBrookfield, Hemingray, Whitall Tatum\n4 Items, Early to Mid-20th Century\nThis collection of four vintage glass utility insulators features classic examples produced for American telegraph, telephone, and power lines. The group includes two embossed Brookfield pieces in deep olive-green glass alongside clear embossed models from Hemingray and Whitall Tatum, showcasing iconic industrial molding details and drip point bases.\nITEMS INCLUDED:\n1.\nBrookfield Glass Insulator\n- Brookfield, dark olive-green glass, embossed \"BROOKFIELD\" and \"NEW YORK\"\n2.\nBrookfield Glass Insulator\n- Brookfield, dark green glass, embossed \"BROOKFIELD\" and \"NEW YORK\" with drip point rim\n3.\nWhitall Tatum Glass Insulator\n- Whitall Tatum Co., clear glass, embossed \"WHITALL TATUM CO. NO. 29\"\n4.\nHemingray Glass Insulator\n- Hemingray, clear glass, embossed \"HEMINGRAY\" with drip point base\nCondition:\nVintage condition consistent with historical outdoor utility service. The green glass insulators have chips along the base rims, and surface staining, residue, and weathering are present across all pieces. No through-cracks or structural failures.\nWarehouse Location: Cleveland\nDue to our lighting, white glare lines may appear on items - This is NOT damage\nIf you have any questions regarding the quality or authenticity of this item or general questions regarding and item, please click Contact Seller on the item page and send us a message. We are available to answer your questions Monday through Friday, 8 am - 3:00 pm, EST.\n* For combined shipping policy see the shipping tab.\nSome items may contain unseen flaws not noted in the description.\nSee Photos. Items sold as-is.",
